					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ia-cope" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5707426); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5707426&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608173196" alt="IA Cope" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5707426)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ia-cope" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5707426); return false;" >IA Cope</a></span> <span class="odate time_1608140051 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">16 Dec 2020 17:34</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4846362">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Cope&nbsp;Crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Let's see what we have here&#8230;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A set of ever-changing anomalous conversation cards that compel the reader to do whatever the card has written on it- for example, if one said &quot;read this card over and over&quot;, the subject would be forced to read the card over and over until the cards are taken from them or they expire.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Mind-affecting objects have been done before, but that doesn't mean you can't put another spin on it. let's see the narrative shall we?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A group of researchers testing the capabilities of the SCP after MTF recovery units with memetic resistance read the cards and are forced to do the actions on the cards, requiring a second team to come in. They are located in a house with a family who is also stuck performing the acts described by the cards. The researchers have extensive testing logs in which they test the capabilities of the cards, ending in a scenario where the last card says &quot;Cause a containment breach at Site-██. &quot; The result box says nothing but [DATA EXPUNGED] resulting in ██ casualties. Testing on SCP-XXXX halted indefinitely.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Okay, this seems kinda boring. So it's only purpose in the narrative is to cause a attainment breach at the end. I mean, the card idea is kinda interesting, depending vastly on what the cards show. I also feel like the last;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>ending in a scenario where the last card says &quot;Cause a containment breach at Site-██. &quot; The result box says nothing but [DATA EXPUNGED] resulting in ██ casualties. Testing on SCP-XXXX halted indefinitely.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>is kinda pointless. I personally don't see why they would have any Foundation personnel using this mind-affecting item, instead per say, a D-Class. I also doubt a D-Class could do much damage.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Although the SCP seems harmless to the researchers at first, the cards in the testing log become more and more malicious as time goes on.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I still don't understand why researchers would use themselves as subjects to the cards in the first place. Even if they did, once testing started to become more malicious I feel like D-Class would come in anyways.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The cards then convey a message to the researchers, ending in something like I KNOW YOU'RE READING THIS : GET AWAY FROM MY CARDS : [EXPLETIVE REMOVED] YOU : Cause a containment breach at Site-██.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Are the cards sapient? If so, why do they do what they do? Are they one entity? Is someone controlling them? Why do the cards exist? If they're just here to make people go crazy and do harmful actions, I just find that boring. Unless you have narrative of course.</p>
<p>Overall Thoughts: &quot;Overall, this has some substance and little to no narrative. First, I suggest you think more about this idea overall. It needs more. So far this is just a thing that does a thing for no reason. That's fine I guess, but very boring. Narrative is what drives a story forward. So, what is the narrative? Did someone create the cards? Are the cards someone? Maybe the cards are an entity's eyes? Also, why are the cards basically evil? Do they have any reason to be? Once you answer these questions, I believe you can go somewhere with this idea. Hope your concept gets better man. PM me if you need help with the concept.</p>
</div>
